# Claude Code — ignore most local agent state, but skills/, rules/ and docs/ are project
# content (custom slash-commands, path-scoped rules and the docs they point at, checked into the repo).
# `**/` keeps it matching at any depth, and excluding the *contents* rather than the
# directory is what lets the negation work — git cannot re-include a path whose parent
# directory is itself excluded, so a bare `.claude/` would silently defeat the negations.
**/.claude/*
!**/.claude/skills/
!**/.claude/rules/
!**/.claude/docs/
